IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-law`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-gate`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-repeal`

-- Tests for il-interpretation-repeal.l4 (Law s 22(1) and (3)).
-- A repeal commencing on 2026-03-01 takes effect at 00:01:00 on that day (Law s 21). Expected values were decided from
-- the words of s 22 before the module was run; a failing assertion is a finding and none was edited to match the code.

§ `Tests: the limits on the force of a repeal`

§§ `s 22(1): a repeal cannot revive what had no validity when it took effect`

`a rule valid from 2010 and never stopped` MEANS `A thing a repeal might be thought to revive` WITH
    `valid from` IS `the moment on` (YMD 2010 1 1) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 0
    `valid until` IS NOTHING

`a rule that stopped at 23:59:59 on 2026-02-28` MEANS `A thing a repeal might be thought to revive` WITH
    `valid from` IS `the moment on` (YMD 2010 1 1) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 0
    `valid until` IS JUST (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 2 28) `at` 23 `:` 59 `:` 59)

`a rule that stopped at 00:00:59 on 2026-03-01` MEANS `A thing a repeal might be thought to revive` WITH
    `valid from` IS `the moment on` (YMD 2010 1 1) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 0
    `valid until` IS JUST (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 59)

`a rule that stopped at 00:01:00 on 2026-03-01` MEANS `A thing a repeal might be thought to revive` WITH
    `valid from` IS `the moment on` (YMD 2010 1 1) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 0
    `valid until` IS JUST (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `at` 0 `:` 1 `:` 0)

`a rule valid only from 00:01:00 on 2026-03-01` MEANS `A thing a repeal might be thought to revive` WITH
    `valid from` IS `the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `at` 0 `:` 1 `:` 0
    `valid until` IS NOTHING

`a rule valid only from 2026-03-02` MEANS `A thing a repeal might be thought to revive` WITH
    `valid from` IS `the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 2) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 0
    `valid until` IS NOTHING

-- tests: L22.1 (the hour test, on both sides of 00:01:00 on the commencement day)
#ASSERT `s 22(1) — the thing had validity at the hour a repeal commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `took effect:` `a rule valid from 2010 and never stopped`
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(1) — the thing had validity at the hour a repeal commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `took effect:` `a rule that stopped at 23:59:59 on 2026-02-28`
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(1) — the thing had validity at the hour a repeal commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `took effect:` `a rule that stopped at 00:00:59 on 2026-03-01`
#ASSERT `s 22(1) — the thing had validity at the hour a repeal commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `took effect:` `a rule that stopped at 00:01:00 on 2026-03-01`
#ASSERT `s 22(1) — the thing had validity at the hour a repeal commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `took effect:` `a rule valid only from 00:01:00 on 2026-03-01`
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(1) — the thing had validity at the hour a repeal commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `took effect:` `a rule valid only from 2026-03-02`
-- The repeal cannot revive what had no validity then; what was valid then is not a case of revival.
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(1) — a repeal commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `revives the thing:` `a rule that stopped at 23:59:59 on 2026-02-28` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(1) — a repeal commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `revives the thing:` `a rule that stopped at 00:00:59 on 2026-03-01` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(1) — a repeal commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `revives the thing:` `a rule valid only from 2026-03-02` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 22(1) — a repeal commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `revives the thing:` `a rule valid from 2010 and never stopped` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` BECAUSE "s 22(1) speaks of a thing that had no validity when the repeal took effect; for a thing that was valid then, the question of reviving it does not arise"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 22(1) — a repeal commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `revives the thing:` `a rule that stopped at 00:01:00 on 2026-03-01` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 22(1) — a repeal commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `revives the thing:` `a rule that stopped at 23:59:59 on 2026-02-28` `, for` `a matter another provision deals with` BECAUSE "the Law is displaced here: another provision deals with the matter, or the matter or its context is inconsistent with the Law, so the Law does not say what the words mean"

§§ `s 22(3): a repeal cannot affect a right or obligation under the repealed law`

`a right under the repealed law` MEANS `A right or obligation` WITH `it arises under the repealed law` IS TRUE
`a right under some other law` MEANS `A right or obligation` WITH `it arises under the repealed law` IS FALSE

-- tests: L22.3
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(3) — a repeal affects the right or obligation:` `a right under the repealed law` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 22(3) — a repeal affects the right or obligation:` `a right under some other law` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` BECAUSE "s 22(3) speaks of a right or obligation under the repealed law"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 22(3) — a repeal affects the right or obligation:` `a right under the repealed law` `, for` `a matter whose context is inconsistent with the Law`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 22(3) — a repeal affects the right or obligation:` `a right under the repealed law` `, for` `a matter another provision deals with`

